From: Surface RT bring-up
Subject: [PATCH 12/12] grate: compile fragment comparisons and conditional selection

Pack the ALU condition field and correct GT/GE encodings. Lower SLT, SGE
and SEQ through conditioned subtraction; add CSEL for TGSI CMP and MAD
addition for ADD. Preserve source modifiers and destination masks. Stage
one of two distinct interpolated inputs for conditional selection, within
the existing two-vec4 temporary budget.

--- a/src/gallium/drivers/grate/fp/fpir.h
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/grate/fp/fpir.h
@@ -23,8 +23,8 @@
 enum fp_condition {
    FP_CONDITION_ALWAYS = 0,
    FP_CONDITION_EQUAL = 1,
-   FP_CONDITION_GEQUAL = 2,
-   FP_CONDITION_GREATER = 3
+   FP_CONDITION_GEQUAL = 3,
+   FP_CONDITION_GREATER = 2
 };
 
 struct fp_alu_dst_operand {
